        "r": 541.5304,
        "b": 434.126101363195
      },
      "content": "Connection of dry contacts: the wiring terminal of dry contacts is located below the interior door of rectifier cabinet. Dry contacts are as shown in Figure 3-15. Dry contacts \"1\" and \"2\" are the wiring terminal for cold start of battery (Note: The terminal carries strong current during the operation of UPS. \"1\" refers to fire wire and \"2\" refers to neutral wire); dry contacts \"4\" and \"5\" are wiring terminals of auxiliary contacts in maintenance bypass (option); dry contact \"6\" and \"7\" for the battery switch undervoltage release wiring terminals.",
